<title>UK: Euro airlines to accept unlimited liability - paper.</title>
<headline>Euro airlines to accept unlimited liability - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>European airlines KLM, SAS, Swissair, Austrian Airlines and Finnair will accept unlimited liability for accidents in which passengers are killed or injured, the Financial Times said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move will do away with the 1929 Warsaw Convention principle of limiting liability. It pre-empts implementation next year of a deal negotiated by the International Air Transportation Association (IATA), dubbed the IATA Intercarrier Agreement, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom + 44 171 542 4367</p>
